**What I changed:**

`src/cache.ts`:
- Added a private `entries` Map backing the cache with `{ value, time }` entries.
- Constructor validates `capacity < 1` and throws `RangeError`.
- Private helpers `isExpired(entry)` (`now() - time >= ttlMs`) and `purgeExpired()` (deletes all expired entries).
- `get`: returns `undefined` for missing/expired (deleting expired), and treats a live hit as a use by deleting + re-inserting the entry.
- `set`: live keys get value replaced and time refreshed without evicting anything; otherwise expired entry removed, `purgeExpired()` runs, LRU entries evicted while `size >= capacity`, then the new entry inserted.
- `has` / `delete`: handle absent and expired cases as specified (deleting expired entries).
- `size` getter: purges expired entries then returns Map size.

`src/cache.test.ts`: Kept the existing "returns what was set" test, added the 9 tests from the spec using a controllable `let t` clock.

